                  text: "Explain physical and emotional changes that characterise puberty",
                  exemplar: "1. Explain the meaning of puberty\n• It is the transition from childhood to adulthood. It occurs between the ages of 10 to 19 (WHO).\n2. Discuss physical and emotional changes that occur at puberty\nPhysical changes in girls at puberty:\n• Growing of pubic hair\n• Menstruation\n• Breasts develop and increase in size\n• Hips widen\n• Change in height, etc.\nPhysical changes in boys at puberty:\n• Pubic hair\n• Break in voice\n• Sperms development\n• Penis grows bigger\n• Change in height etc.\nEmotional changes in both sexes:\n• Curiosity\n• Adventurous\n• Conflict of identity (not child, not adult)\n• Mood swings\n• Development of the urge to have sex, etc.\nLearners to write their concerns relating to puberty anonymously and place them in a box. The teacher discusses these concerns in class to address any fears or misconceptions about puberty.",
